.TH SDL_WriteStorageFile 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_WriteStorageFile \- Synchronously write a file from client memory into a storage container.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_storage.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_WriteStorageFile(SDL_Storage *storage, const char *path, const void *source, Uint64 length);
.fi
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I storage
a storage container to write to\[char46]
.TP
.I path
the relative path of the file to write\[char46]
.TP
.I source
a client-provided buffer to write from\[char46]
.TP
.I length
the length of the source buffer\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true if the file was written or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

